    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0138" n="44" xml:id="pg44"/>

                <head>No. 43.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Bounder de
                        Melsbroeck</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 25,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 21st
                    ultimo relative to the international congress of commercial law, which is to be
                    held at Brussels in September next, I have the honor to inform you that David
                    Dudley Field, esq., of New York, has been duly appointed as American delegate to
                    the congress in question.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
